{{!
    @template block_compass/page

    The block's content on its own page (ADR-012, decision 1): a wrapper carrying the class
    core puts on the block's section, block_compass, which is the one class the stylesheet is
    scoped to - and not core's block card chrome, which is drawer furniture with an instance id
    behind it - around the block template as a partial, fed the same props.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * props - the component's props, JSON-encoded by block_compass\output\page: the block's,
      with headinglevel 2.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "props": "{\"labels\": {\"loaderror\": \"Your courses could not be loaded.\"}, \"strips\": [], \"headinglevel\": 2}"
    }
}}
<div class="block_compass compass-page">
    {{> block_compass/block }}
</div>
